  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b000001",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 1,
      "end_line": 1,
      "raw": "# FileProvider compatibility\n",
      "level": 1,
      "title": "FileProvider compatibility"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000002",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 2,
      "end_line": 2,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 3,
      "end_line": 8,
      "raw": "`iiFileProvider::Compatibility` is a source-composed, Qt-free C++23 bridge for\nthe existing `.iisacc-lock` writer protocol. `FileWriteLock` reserves the lock\npath exclusively, retains a platform lock/handle for its lifetime and publishes\nthe existing PID/application/hostname metadata. Native and former Qt writers\ntherefore exclude one another. `writeCompatible` holds that guard while the\nNative provider stages and atomically publishes complete replacement bytes.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000004",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 9,
      "end_line": 9,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 10,
      "end_line": 13,
      "raw": "Only a proven dead process on the same host is eligible for stale-lock recovery.\nThe bridge verifies the held file identity before removing it and never removes\nan active, foreign-host, malformed or unidentifiable owner's guard. It does not\nadd a Qt library or header dependency and does not alter the installed provider.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000006",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 14,
      "end_line": 14,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 15,
      "end_line": 20,
      "raw": "Congregation composes this target from source, exercises native exclusion and\ndead-owner recovery without Qt, and uses QLockFile only as an independent test\noracle for compatibility in both directions. Windows MSVC x64 also builds and\nruns `iiFileProvider.Compatibility.Contracts`, including repeated atomic\nreplacement and lock cleanup. This Windows check is distinct from Congregation's\nmacOS bidirectional Qt oracle. See [Windows verification](../docs/WindowsCompatibility.md).\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000008",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 21,
      "end_line": 21,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000009",
      "kind": "html",
      "start_line": 22,
      "end_line": 22,
      "raw": "<!-- workspace-docs:readme:start -->\n"
    },
